<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0ad8ada2c9fc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4374] After lengthy legal proceedings, the accused was sentenced to nine years imprisonment, with a non-parole period of 5.5 years, by Judge Culver in the District Court at the Downing Centre." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4374" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1086e5e6da07> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Andrew Thomas Hayler might have been one of Hannah's most trusted friends for over a decade, yet behind the façade of friendship, he had been orchestrating a two-year campaign of online abuse." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4379" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/26209043abde> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police finally arrested Hayler in August 2022, after six months of Ms Grundy living fear of being attacked by him or a stranger who'd seen the videos." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/26b6468d7c75> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Teacher’s shock discovery: Close friend responsible for sharing her deepfake porn images" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/352782738d25> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Andrew Thomas Hayler had been using social media photos of his victims, superimposing their faces onto explicit pornographic images, and uploading these altered images to an Instagram account and a pornographic website with over 300,000 members." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4379" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/45547e3b8622> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It tells a shocking story of online abuse and AI generated pornographic images." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4374" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/56a9c40d8d08> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "They later discovered the website was found by a New Zealand private investigator who realised the danger its content had put Ms Grundy in." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5d170b0bd941> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hannah's ordeal began in August 2022 when she discovered violent, degrading AI-generated pornographic content of herself." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4374" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/608bbe8e1c7f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4366] Andrew Thomas Hayler pleaded guilty to 28 counts of using a carriage service to cause offence involving 26 women between July 2020 and August 2022, including his close friends, former housemates and colleagues." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/628bdfdc4e33> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "'I found deepfake porn of myself online. Then I found out who was responsible.'" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4379" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/668682eee6b3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Even though the photos and videos had been created with AI by superimposing Ms Grundy's face onto other women..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6787a650296b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "How a young Aussie teacher became the target of vile deepfake images" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/76b12387e48f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Some of the pictures were incredibly graphic and used AI technology to add features such as bruising." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4376" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7a5536601da8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hannah found deepfake porn of herself online. But the most disturbing revelation was still to come" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4373" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7b305b9e8a3b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Some were really crude, but others used AI, and there were even GIFs, moving images of violent porn with my face on them." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4379" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/80b184c2bc5b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4379] Andrew Thomas Hayler might have been one of Hannah's most trusted friends for over a decade, yet behind the façade of friendship, he had been orchestrating a two-year campaign of online abuse. [4373] Rachel McGinty described finding out that Hayler had created a thread on the website called \"Let's r*pe Rachel\"." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4379" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/84965eab475b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After lengthy legal proceedings, the accused was sentenced to nine years imprisonment, with a non-parole period of 5.5 years, by Judge Culver in the District Court at the Downing Centre." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4374" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8bf309fb1433> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Some of the pictures were incredibly graphic and used AI technology to add features such as bruising." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8ea03a224e57> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hannah's case is a tragic example of the damage caused by online anonymity, AI manipulation, and the failure of early intervention." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4374" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/92ab1cdfe93a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4366] Andrew Thomas Hayler pleaded guilty to 28 counts of using a carriage service to cause offence involving 26 women between July 2020 and August 2022, including his close friends, former housemates and colleagues. [4375] 6 women fronted Hayler in court to described how his weaponised usage of deepfakes had impacted their lives with one, Jessica Stuart, saying he'd 'incited a whole community of predators against us'." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/94e55042aebb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Andrew Thomas Hayler had been using social media photos of his victims, superimposing their faces onto explicit pornographic images, and uploading these altered images to an Instagram account and a pornographic website with over 300,000 members." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4379" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/955fbba627fa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hannah realised that the pictures had been taken from her Facebook and Instagram, which were both private, meaning that the person behind the deep fake images was one of her mates." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4376" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9e8634b5d829> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4375] Hannah Grundy received a series of anonymous emails in February 2022 warning several pornographic images of her had been shared on a website. [4373] the posts of Hannah were incredibly graphic in nature, using AI technology to add things like bruising." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b3970183bffd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After receiving no significant action from the police, Sidnie Sarang intervened to help Hannah push for justice. It was a long and arduous process, but the perpetrator was finally arrested." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4374" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bd5e24b2d68a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But over the next two months, similar emails followed, warning her that this man, from Sydney University was posting explicit photos of her online." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4379" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d2fa3aed8b51> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Shock over revenge porn sicko: ‘Best friend’" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4376" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d50b6f1ccc52> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Andrew Thomas Hayler had been using social media photos of his victims, superimposing their faces onto explicit pornographic images, and uploading these altered images to an Instagram account and a pornographic website with over 300,000 members." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4379" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/da3baa249008> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "the posts of Hannah were incredibly graphic in nature, using AI technology to add things like bruising." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4373" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f7b1c67ab8a3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Andrew Thomas Hayler pleaded guilty to 28 counts of using a carriage service to cause offence involving 26 women between July 2020 and August 2022, including his close friends, former housemates and colleagues." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fc7878d01290> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Justice for Hannah Grundy – A Landmark Victory Against Online Abuse For Our Client" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4374" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/Risk/2cdd96a30b0c> a airo:Risk ;
    rdfs:label "Risk of AI-generated non-consensual intimate imagery and online harassment" ;
    airo:confidenceScore "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    airo:extractionMode "abstracted" ;
    airo:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f6d79a7d5a78> ;
    airo:hasSourceDocument <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/document/4375> ;
    airo:leadsTo <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/Consequence/c3fff0e594c2> .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3c07facac414> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Jessica Stuart, who had considered Hayler a 'close friend', spoke about the horror of learning he had shared photographs of her plastered with degrading comments." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4373" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/42de53b5fd10> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Even though the photos and videos had been created with AI by superimposing Ms Grundy's face onto other women..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7103d3bfb55a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Australia's criminal code was amended in August to sentence anyone found guilty of creating 'non-consensual deepfake sexually explicit material' to up to seven years in prison." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f6d79a7d5a78> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "6 women fronted Hayler in court to described how his weaponised usage of deepfakes had impacted their lives with one, Jessica Stuart, saying he'd 'incited a whole community of predators against us'." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/029fbcf86bb6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "They approached criminal lawyer Sidnie Sarang, who started to build a case against Andy while he continued to post sexual images of Hannah online." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4376" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/073953e5bb2a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "They approached criminal lawyer Sidnie Sarang, who started to build a case against Andy while he continued to post sexual images of Hannah online." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/121bf95e8931> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Judge Jane Culver sentenced Hayler to nine years in prison with a non-parole period of five-and-a-half years." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1a8ee4766051> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Rachel McGinty described finding out that Hayler had created a thread on the website called \"Let's r*pe Rachel\"." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4373" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1ae5bc8545a6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "She asked her partner Kris to open the link for her while she watched on." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4376" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2247ad324a44> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "6 women fronted Hayler in court to described how his weaponised usage of deepfakes had impacted their lives with one, Jessica Stuart, saying he'd 'incited a whole community of predators against us'." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4c4f14a0dc16> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It was a New Zealand-based private investigator and former police officer named Will who spotted the photographs of Hannah." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4373" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/62e9d12d0797> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "She asked her partner Kris to open the link for her while she watched on." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/693e7ddf33de> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police finally arrested Hayler in August 2022, after six months of Ms Grundy living fear of being attacked by him or a stranger who'd seen the videos." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7686d8877124> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On their lawyer's advice, they recruited forensic computing expert Allan Watt to compile a report bolstering their assertion that Hayler was the perpetrator." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4373" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/85fd65f03412> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Armed with a trove of digital evidence, she and Kris went to Newtown Police Station to report what they had found." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4373" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9c72781be2ee> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When high school teacher Hannah Grundy received a series of cryptic emails, she never imagined they would lead her to uncover a deeply disturbing internet hate crime." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4379" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a702eed27789> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Andy Hayler was a superviser at Manning Bar when Hannah started there as a student." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4376" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ac5f411cd174> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Andrew Thomas Hayler might have been one of Hannah's most trusted friends for over a decade, yet behind the façade of friendship, he had been orchestrating a two-year campaign of online abuse." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4379" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bec1319ff3b4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The next day Hannah and Kris went to the police with their evidence, but cops said it wasn't enough to charge Andy." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4376" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c01af5958ed2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When science teacher Hannah Grundy started receiving emails from a stranger called John Doe, she assumed it was a scam and decided to ignore them." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cc937a862f03> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It became more and more obvious that it was our friend Andy, said Kris." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cfa4989798d6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Judge Jane Culver described Hayler's actions as a \"vivid and dangerous illustration\" of the way violence was perpetrated online." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4373" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d5879a7e40da> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Our top Criminal Lawyer, Sidnie Sarang, represented Hannah through this harrowing ordeal." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4374" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d8c92dc4ea2b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Andrew Thomas Hayler pleaded guilty to 28 counts of using a carriage service to cause offence involving 26 women between July 2020 and August 2022, including his close friends, former housemates and colleagues." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dd909fb253d1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "the couple realized the attacker was someone very close to them- Andrew Hayler." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/04cf4c9bf432> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After lengthy legal proceedings, the accused was sentenced to nine years imprisonment, with a non-parole period of 5.5 years, by Judge Culver in the District Court at the Downing Centre." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4374" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/00272b2f7c44> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 was Rachel McGinty and another was Jessica Stuart, who had both worked at a university bar with Hannah and her partner Kris, and were part of their tight knit friendship group." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4376" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/125588bddb32> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hannah Grundy received a series of anonymous emails in February 2022 warning several pornographic images of her had been shared on a website." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4375" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a8fb97563277> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 was Rachel McGinty and another was Jessica Stuart, who had both worked at a university bar with Hannah and her partner Kris, and were part of their tight-knit friendship group." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4366" .

